{"id":"mahabharata-6-111","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":111,"title":"एकादशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 111 · The tenth day: the plan to fell Bhishma","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how Bhishma fought on the tenth day. Sanjaya tells how Bhishma, wishing his own death, refused to strike the great Pandava heroes, and how the Pandavas put Shikhandin and Arjuna at the front to bring him down.","kn":"ಹತ್ತನೇ ದಿನ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡಿದನೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತನ್ನ ಸಾವನ್ನು ಬಯಸಿದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಮಹಾ ಪಾಂಡವ ವೀರರನ್ನು ಹೊಡೆಯದಿದ್ದುದನ್ನೂ, ಪಾಂಡವರು ಶಿಖಂಡಿ ಮತ್ತು ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ಮುಂದಿಟ್ಟು ಅವನನ್ನು ಉರುಳಿಸಲು ಯತ್ನಿಸಿದ್ದನ್ನೂ ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि दसवें दिन भीष्म कैसे लड़े। संजय बताते हैं कि अपनी मृत्यु चाहने वाले भीष्म ने बड़े पाण्डव वीरों पर प्रहार नहीं किया, और पाण्डवों ने शिखण्डी और अर्जुन को आगे रखकर उन्हें गिराने का प्रयत्न किया।","te":"పదవ రోజు భీష్ముడు ఎలా పోరాడాడని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. తన మరణాన్ని కోరిన భీష్ముడు పాండవ మహావీరులను కొట్టకపోవడాన్ని, పాండవులు శిఖండిని, అర్జునుని ముందుంచి అతన్ని కూల్చడానికి ప్రయత్నించడాన్ని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"பத்தாம் நாள் பீஷ்மர் எவ்வாறு போரிட்டார் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். தன் மரணத்தை விரும்பிய பீஷ்மர் பெரும் பாண்டவ வீரரைத் தாக்காததையும், பாண்டவர் சிகண்டியையும் அர்ஜுனனையும் முன்வைத்து அவரை வீழ்த்த முயன்றதையும் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"പത്താം ദിവസം ഭീഷ്മർ എങ്ങനെ പൊരുതി എന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. സ്വന്തം മരണം ആഗ്രഹിച്ച ഭീഷ്മർ മഹാവീരരായ പാണ്ഡവരെ പ്രഹരിക്കാതിരുന്നതും, അദ്ദേഹത്തെ വീഴ്ത്താൻ പാണ്ഡവർ ശിഖണ്ഡിയെയും അർജുനനെയും മുന്നിൽ നിർത്തിയതും സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.111; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कथं शांतनवो भीष्मो दशमेऽहनि संजय ।\nअयुध्यत महावीर्यैः पाण्डवैः सहसृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, how did Bhishma, the son of Shantanu, fight on the tenth day against the mighty Pandavas and the Srinjayas?"}},{"n":2,"text":"कुरवश्च कथं युद्धे पाण्डवान्प्रत्यवारयन् ।\nआचक्ष्व मे महायुद्धं भीष्मस्याहवशोभिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how did the Kauravas hold back the Pandavas in the battle? Tell me of the great battle of Bhishma, who shone in war."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"कुरवः पाण्डवैः सार्धं यथायुध्यन्त भारत ।\nयथा च तदभूद्युद्धं तत्ते वक्ष्यामि शृण्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear, Bharata, how the Kurus fought with the Pandavas and how that battle went; I will tell it to you as you listen."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रेषिताः परलोकाय परमास्त्रैः किरीटिना ।\nअहन्यहनि संप्राप्तास्तावकानां रथव्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Day after day the companies of your chariot-warriors were sent to the next world by the supreme weapons of Arjuna, the wearer of the diadem."}},{"n":5,"text":"यथाप्रतिज्ञं कौरव्यः स चापि समितिंजयः ।\nपार्थानामकरोद्भीष्मः सततं समितिक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma of the Kuru line, victor in battles, kept to his vow and relentlessly caused slaughter among the sons of Pritha in battle."}},{"n":6,"text":"कुरुभिः सहितं भीष्मं युध्यमानं महारथम् ।\nअर्जुनं च सपाञ्चाल्यं दृष्ट्वा संशयिता जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhishma fighting with the Kurus, and Arjuna with the Panchalas, people were in doubt about the outcome."}},{"n":7,"text":"दशमेऽहनि तस्मिंस्तु भीष्मार्जुनसमागमे ।\nअवर्तत महारौद्रः सततं समितिक्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On that tenth day, when Bhishma and Arjuna met, a most dreadful, unbroken slaughter went on."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्मिन्नयुतशो राजन्भूयश्च स परंतपः ।\nभीष्मः शांतनवो योधाञ्जघान परमास्त्रवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that battle, king, Bhishma the son of Shantanu, scourge of foes and master of supreme weapons, killed warriors by tens of thousands and more."}},{"n":9,"text":"येषामज्ञातकल्पानि नामगोत्राणि पार्थिव ।\nते हतास्तत्र भीष्मेण शूराः सर्वेऽनिवर्तिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many brave men, king, who never turned back and whose names and clans were hardly known, were killed there by Bhishma."}},{"n":10,"text":"दशाहानि ततस्तप्त्वा भीष्मः पाण्डववाहिनीम् ।\nनिरविद्यत धर्मात्मा जीवितेन परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After burning the Pandava army for ten days, the righteous Bhishma, scourge of foes, grew weary of life."}},{"n":11,"text":"स क्षिप्रं वधमन्विच्छन्नात्मनोऽभिमुखं रणे ।\nन हन्यां मानवश्रेष्ठान्संग्रामेऽभिमुखानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing for a swift death, he thought, \"I must not kill the best of men in battle when they face me directly.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा महाबाहुः पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nअभ्याशस्थं महाराज पाण्डवं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having thought so, your father Devavrata, the mighty-armed, spoke these words to the Pandava Yudhishthira, who stood nearby."}},{"n":13,"text":"युधिष्ठिर महाप्राज्ञ सर्वशास्त्रविशारद ।\nशृणु मे वचनं तात धर्म्यं स्वर्ग्यं च जल्पतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Yudhishthira, very wise one, expert in all the scriptures, listen to the words I speak, my son, which are righteous and lead to heaven."}},{"n":14,"text":"निर्विण्णोऽस्मि भृशं तात देहेनानेन भारत ।\nघ्नतश्च मे गतः कालः सुबहून्प्राणिनो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am deeply weary of this body, my son, and my time has gone in killing a great many creatures in battle."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्मात्पार्थं पुरोधाय पाञ्चालान्सृञ्जयांस्तथा ।\nमद्वधे क्रियतां यत्नो मम चेदिच्छसि प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, if you wish to please me, put Arjuna in front with the Panchalas and Srinjayas, and make an effort to kill me.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"तस्य तन्मतमाज्ञाय पाण्डवः सत्यदर्शनः ।\nभीष्मं प्रतिययौ यत्तः संग्रामे सह सृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding his wish, the Pandava Yudhishthira, who sees the truth, advanced carefully against Bhishma in the battle with the Srinjayas."}},{"n":17,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्ततो राजन्पाण्डवश्च युधिष्ठिरः ।\nश्रुत्वा भीष्मस्य तां वाचं चोदयामासतुर्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Dhrishtadyumna and the Pandava Yudhishthira, having heard Bhishma's words, urged their army on."}},{"n":18,"text":"अभिद्रवत युध्यध्वं भीष्मं जयत संयुगे ।\nरक्षिताः सत्यसंधेन जिष्णुना रिपुजिष्णुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"They said, \"Charge! Fight! Defeat Bhishma in battle! You are protected by Arjuna, true to his word and conqueror of enemies."}},{"n":19,"text":"अयं चापि महेष्वासः पार्षतो वाहिनीपतिः ।\nभीमसेनश्च समरे पालयिष्यति वो ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great archer, Dhrishtadyumna the son of Prishata, the army's leader, and Bhimasena will surely guard you in the fight."}},{"n":20,"text":"न वै भीष्माद्भयं किंचित्कर्तव्यं युधि सृञ्जयाः ।\nध्रुवं भीष्मं विजेष्यामः पुरस्कृत्य शिखण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Srinjayas, you need fear nothing at all from Bhishma in this battle. We shall surely conquer Bhishma with Shikhandi in front.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तथा तु समयं कृत्वा दशमेऽहनि पाण्डवाः ।\nब्रह्मलोकपरा भूत्वा संजग्मुः क्रोधमूर्छिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made that resolve, on the tenth day the Pandavas, aiming at the world of Brahma and maddened with anger, advanced together."}},{"n":22,"text":"शिखण्डिनं पुरस्कृत्य पाण्डवं च धनंजयम् ।\nभीष्मस्य पातने यत्नं परमं ते समास्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Putting Shikhandi and the Pandava Arjuna in front, they made a supreme effort to bring Bhishma down."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततस्तव सुतादिष्टा नानाजनपदेश्वराः ।\nद्रोणेन सहपुत्रेण सहसेना महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, ordered by your son, the lords of many realms, mighty men with their forces, together with Drona and his son,"}},{"n":24,"text":"दुःशासनश्च बलवान्सह सर्वैः सहोदरैः ।\nभीष्मं समरमध्यस्थं पालयां चक्रिरे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the powerful Duhshasana with all his brothers, protected Bhishma where he stood in the middle of the battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्तु तावकाः शूराः पुरस्कृत्य यतव्रतम् ।\nशिखण्डिप्रमुखान्पार्थान्योधयन्ति स्म संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your brave men, placing Bhishma of firm vows in front, fought the sons of Pritha who were led by Shikhandi."}},{"n":26,"text":"चेदिभिश्च सपाञ्चालैः सहितो वानरध्वजः ।\nययौ शांतनवं भीष्मं पुरस्कृत्य शिखण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna of the ape banner, with the Chedis and Panchalas, went against Bhishma the son of Shantanu, with Shikhandi in front."}},{"n":27,"text":"द्रोणपुत्रं शिनेर्नप्ता धृष्टकेतुस्तु पौरवम् ।\nयुधामन्युः सहामात्यं दुर्योधनमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtaketu fought Drona's son, and Shini's grandson Satyaki fought the Paurava Bhurishravas; Yudhamanyu fought Duryodhana together with his counselors."}},{"n":28,"text":"विराटस्तु सहानीकः सहसेनं जयद्रथम् ।\nवृद्धक्षत्रस्य दायादमाससाद परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata with his troops approached Jayadratha and his army, Jayadratha the heir of Vriddhakshatra, and Virata was a scourge of foes."}},{"n":29,"text":"मद्रराजं महेष्वासं सहसैन्यं युधिष्ठिरः ।\nभीमसेनाभिगुप्तश्च नागानीकमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, guarded by Bhimasena, attacked the great archer, the king of Madra, with his army and his elephant ranks."}},{"n":30,"text":"अप्रधृष्यमनावार्यं सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरम् ।\nद्रोणं प्रति ययौ यत्तः पाञ्चाल्यः सह सोमकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The prince of Panchala, with the Somakas, went intently against Drona, who was hard to overcome, impossible to stop, and the best of all who bear weapons."}},{"n":31,"text":"कर्णिकारध्वजं चापि सिंहकेतुररिंदमः ।\nप्रत्युज्जगाम सौभद्रं राजपुत्रो बृहद्बलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prince Brihadbala, whose banner shows a lion, went against Abhimanyu, Subhadra's son, whose banner has the karnikara flower."}},{"n":32,"text":"शिखण्डिनं च पुत्रास्ते पाण्डवं च धनंजयम् ।\nराजभिः समरे सार्धमभिपेतुर्जिघांसवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons and the other kings, eager to kill, fell upon Shikhandi and the Pandava Arjuna in the battle."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्मिन्नतिमहाभीमे सेनयोर्वै पराक्रमे ।\nसंप्रधावत्स्वनीकेषु मेदिनी समकम्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the two armies rushed forward in that very terrible clash, the earth shook."}},{"n":34,"text":"तान्यनीकान्यनीकेषु समसज्जन्त भारत ।\nतावकानां परेषां च दृष्ट्वा शांतनवं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the son of Shantanu in the battle, the divisions of your side and the enemy's closed with each other, O Bharata."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्तेषां प्रयततामन्योन्यमभिधावताम् ।\nप्रादुरासीन्महाञ्शब्दो दिक्षु सर्वासु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they strove and charged at each other, a great sound arose in all directions, Bharata."}},{"n":36,"text":"शङ्खदुन्दुभिघोषैश्च वारणानां च बृंहितैः ।\nसिंहनादैश्च सैन्यानां दारुणः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"It became dreadful with the blare of conches and drums, the trumpeting of elephants and the lion-roars of the troops."}},{"n":37,"text":"सा च सर्वनरेन्द्राणां चन्द्रार्कसदृशी प्रभा ।\nवीराङ्गदकिरीटेषु निष्प्रभा समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The radiance of all the kings, which was like that of the moon and the sun, grew dull on their warriors' armlets and crowns."}},{"n":38,"text":"रजोमेघाश्च संजज्ञुः शस्त्रविद्युद्भिरावृताः ।\nधनुषां चैव निर्घोषो दारुणः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Clouds of dust arose, wrapped in the lightning of weapons, and the terrible twang of bows rang out."}},{"n":39,"text":"बाणशङ्खप्रणादाश्च भेरीणां च महास्वनाः ।\nरथघोषश्च संजग्मुः सेनयोरुभयोरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whistling of arrows, the sound of conches, the great booming of kettledrums and the rumble of chariots rose from both armies."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रासशक्त्यृष्टिसंघैश्च बाणौघैश्च समाकुलम् ।\nनिष्प्रकाशमिवाकाशं सेनयोः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sky above the armies, thick with masses of lances, spears, javelins and showers of arrows, seemed to lose its light."}},{"n":41,"text":"अन्योन्यं रथिनः पेतुर्वाजिनश्च महाहवे ।\nकुञ्जराः कुञ्जराञ्जघ्नुः पदातींश्च पदातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteers and horses fell upon each other in the great fight; elephants struck elephants, and foot soldiers struck foot soldiers."}},{"n":42,"text":"तदासीत्सुमहद्युद्धं कुरूणां पाण्डवैः सह ।\nभीष्महेतोर्नरव्याघ्र श्येनयोरामिषे यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kurus and the Pandavas fought a huge battle for Bhishma's sake, O tiger among men, like two hawks over a piece of meat."}},{"n":43,"text":"तयोः समागमो घोरो बभूव युधि भारत ।\nअन्योन्यस्य वधार्थाय जिगीषूणां रणाजिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A terrible meeting of the two sides took place in that battle, O Bharata, as men eager to win on the field sought to kill each other."}}]}]}